      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"table_id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING_HIST\", \"table_name\": \"FCLT_BUILDING_HIST\", \"count\": 10, \"items\": [{\"metric_id\": \"dw_12\", \"name\": \"Building Type Ownership Rollup of Historical Room Count Statistics for MIT Non-Residential Buildings\", \"category\": \"Facility Space Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each building type, show the building type name, the ownership type, and calculate the average, range, and variance of the number of rooms in building history records for buildings of that type and ownership type that are located on the MIT site, but exclude buildings that are classified as residential. For each building type, include a grand total for all ownership types in the format of (building type, null, total statistics). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_76\", \"name\": \"Stata Center Floor Assignable and Non-Assignable Area Totals for MIT Academic Buildings with 50+ Historical Rooms\", \"category\": \"Facility Space Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For all buildings on the MIT site that are academic buildings with more than 50 rooms (according to the building history) and are specifically the Ray and Maria Stata Center, list each floor's number, the total assignable area on that floor, and the total non-assignable area, ordered by floor number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_126\", \"name\": \"Cambridge Residential Buildings Above Average Gross Area with Address and Historical Room Statistics\", \"category\": \"Facility Space Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For building addresses in the city of CAMBRIDGE that are used as a residence, show the building number from the address, the address purpose, the city, the postal code, the building name, the building type, the building use, the building's gross area, the fiscal period from the building history, the number of rooms from the building history, and the minimum assignable area from the building history over each building key group, but only for those buildings whose gross area is greater than the average gross area of all resident buildings in CAMBRIDGE (excluding buildings named \\\"Ashdown\\\"), ordered by building key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_505\", \"name\": \"MIT Academic Building Historical Assignable Area Stddev and Average Non-Assignable Area\", \"category\": \"Facility Space Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each building, what is the building name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the assignable area across its historical records, and the average non-assignable area across its historical records, considering only buildings with more than 3 historical records, with a nonzero assignable area, and that are academic buildings? Additionally, restrict the results to buildings at MIT. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1190\", \"name\": \"Academic Building Historical Assignable Area Stddev with Room Area Average and Variance\", \"category\": \"Facility Space Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each building where the building type is 'ACADEMIC', the building is not the Brown Building, and the building has more than 3 historical records, give the building name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the assignable area across its historical records, the average area of its rooms, and the variance of the area of its rooms, including only buildings that are academic buildings or have building number '32'. List the results in descending order of the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the assignable area. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1357\", \"name\": \"Access Level Campus Sector Room Count Variance Rollup with Fairchild Floor Room Area Statistics\", \"category\": \"Facility Space Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each access level code and campus sector, what is the access level code, access level name, campus sector, the variance of the number of rooms in the building history for buildings with a nonzero number of rooms, assignable area greater than 0, and that are residential buildings at MIT, as well as, for each floor in the Fairchild Building with access level 1 or 2 and in academic buildings, the floor number, the building's long name, the range and variance of the area of rooms on that floor? Only include buildings that are at MIT. Also, include subtotals for each access level code (the corresponding campus sector field is 'SUBTOTAL') and a grand total across all access level codes (the corresponding campus sector field is 'TOTAL'). Do not repeat the access level code if it is the same as the previous row. Sort the table by access level code, campus sector, and floor. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1488\", \"name\": \"MIT Academic Building Floor Room Area Statistics with Assignable Area Dispersion and Room Counts\", \"category\": \"Facility Space Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic building at MIT and each of its floors with total assignable area greater than 5000 and at least one room with access level 1 or 2, provide the building's long name, the floor number, the range and variance of the area of rooms on that floor (considering only rooms with access level 1 or 2), the range and variance of the assignable area of its floors that have at least one room, and the total number of rooms in the building. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1888\", \"name\": \"Cambridge Academic Building History Statistics Matched with MIT Room Area Dispersion\", \"category\": \"Facility Space Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic building in Cambridge, MA (excluding the Stata building), with more than 1 room and a non-null building name, and that is also an academic building at MIT with more than 10 rooms, show the building key, building name, building type, the number of historical records, the total assignable area across all historical records, the average number of rooms per historical record, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the areas of its rooms, and the total assignable area of the building at MIT, considering only buildings that satisfy all these criteria. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2596\", \"name\": \"Top 10 Buildings by Historical Record Count with Building Type and Campus Sector\", \"category\": \"Facility Space Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 building names with the highest number of historical records, list the building name, the number of historical records, the building type, and the campus sector. Do not repeat the building name if it is the same as the previous row. Sort the table by the number of historical records in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_488\", \"name\": \"MIT Academic Building Use with Largest Room Area Variance and Largest Total Area Building\", \"category\": \"Facility Space Analysis\", \"desc\": \"Among all academic buildings at MIT, which building use type has the largest variance in room area, and what is the name of the building with the largest total room area for that use type? Show the building use, the area variance, and the building name with the largest total room area for that use type. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}"
