ignable_area`, `column_concept_fiscal_period`, `column_concept_building_type_site`, `column_concept_num_of_rooms`, `column_concept_access_level` — all retrieved; key content cited in Sections 3 and 6.\n\n**Metrics (precedents):** dw_488, dw_505, dw_1888, dw_126, dw_12, dw_1357, dw_1488, dw_76, dw_1190, dw_2596 (all consume FCLT_BUILDING_HIST); dw_3280, dw_3867 (running-sum window precedents).\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- Graph on FCLT_BUILDING_HIST: joins ↔ FCLT_BUILDING (incoming), → FCLT_ROOMS, → FCLT_FLOOR; concept member of `concept_building_inventory`; column_concepts: building_type_site, num_of_rooms, assignable_area, access_level, fiscal_period. 10 metrics depend on it (dw_12, dw_76, dw_126, dw_505, dw_1190, dw_1357, dw_1488, dw_1888, dw_2596, dw_488).\n- FCLT_ROOMS → FCLT_MAJOR_USE via `FCLT_MAJOR_USE_KEY` (documented in both tables' column descs).\n- **dw_488 precedent SQL** joins `FCLT_ROOMS r JOIN FCLT_BUILDING_HIST b ON r.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY = b.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY` with filters `b.BUILDING_TYPE='ACADEMIC' AND b.SITE='MIT'` and computes `SUM(r.AREA)` as \"total room area\" — the exact join path and filter style this task needs.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (building source):**\n| Dimension | FCLT_BUILDING_HIST | FCLT_BUILDING | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | building × fiscal period (48 periods) | building (current) | table descs |\n| FISCAL_PERIOD column | yes | **no** | columns list |\n| Per-period ASSIGNABLE_AREA / EXT_GROSS_AREA / CAMPUS_SECTOR | yes | current only | columns list |\n| OWNERSHIP_TYPE | yes ('OWNED'/'LEASED') | yes | columns list |\n| Family | FCLT_* (joins FCLT_ROOMS) | FCLT_* | concept_building_inventory comparisons |\n\n**Room source:** FCLT_ROOMS (full current inventory, AREA in m²) vs FCLT_ROOMS_HIST (only 201505 — VIOLATES the 48-period requirement) vs FAC_ROOMS (wrong key family) vs SPACE_DETAIL (square feet, no major-use keys).\n\n**Use filter:** FCLT_MAJOR_USE.MAJOR_USE explicitly lists 'LABS' and 'RESIDENT' codes; FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST only covers 201505; FAC_MAJOR_USE is the wrong family.\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness:**\n- Fiscal period output → FCLT_BUILDING_HIST: SUPPORTED; FCLT_BUILDING: NOT-SUPPORTED (no column).\n- Running sum of assignable area per campus sector → hist `ASSIGNABLE_AREA` + `CAMPUS_SECTOR` per period: SUPPORTED.\n- External gross area → hist `EXT_GROSS_AREA` (\"Extended gross area … at the fiscal period\"): SUPPORTED.\n- OWNED / ACADEMIC / SITE='MIT' filters → both tables SUPPORTED; hist applies per-period (dw_488 precedent filters on hist).\n- RESIDENT/LABS room area → FCLT_ROOMS+FCLT_MAJOR_USE: SUPPORTED; FCLT_ROOMS_HIST: NOT-SUPPORTED (single period).\n- Exclude Stata → `FCLT_BUILDING_KEY <> '32'` (dw_1888 precedent: \"excluding the Stata building\" → `b.FCLT_BUILDING_KEY <> 32`): SUPPORTED.\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:** \"fiscal period\"→FCLT_BUILDING_HIST.FISCAL_PERIOD; \"owned by MIT\"→OWNERSHIP_TYPE='OWNED' (only 'OWNED'/'LEASED' domain); \"academic building\"→BUILDING_TYPE='ACADEMIC'; \"at MIT\"→SITE='MIT'; \"external gross area\"→EXT_GROSS_AREA (unique lexical match); \"campus sector\"→CAMPUS_SECTOR; \"RESIDENT or LABS purposes\"→FCLT_MAJOR_USE.MAJOR_USE IN ('RESIDENT','LABS') (codes cited verbatim in table desc); \"total room area greater than 1000\"→HAVING SUM(r.AREA)>1000 on the room join (dw_488 uses SUM(r.AREA) as \"total room area\").\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:** Academic-MIT-building + room-area precedents on FCLT_BUILDING_HIST: dw_488 (SUM(r.AREA) per building), dw_1488, dw_1190; on FCLT_BUILDING: dw_505, dw_1888 (current-snapshot measures). Running-sum window precedents: dw_3280/dw_3867 — `SUM(x) OVER (PARTITION BY group ORDER BY key)`. Stata-exclusion precedent: dw_1888 (`FCLT_BUILDING_KEY <> 32`).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\nFCLT_BUILDING_HIST is the fiscal-period building analysis table (10 metrics: area/room-count trends, dispersion across history). FCLT_ROOMS+FCLT_MAJOR_USE serve room-use area statistics (dw_488, dw_3332, dw_4776). FCLT_BUILDING serves current-attribute questions (dw_505, dw_1888 subq2).\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\nInvestigated via semantic_get/semantic_graph/mysql_query attempts: FCLT_BUILDING_HIST ✔ (get, neighbors, metrics_by_table), FCLT_BUILDING ✔, FCLT_ROOMS ✔, FCLT_MAJOR_USE ✔, FCLT_ROOMS_HIST ✔, FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST ✔, FAC_* / BUILDINGS / SPACE_* / ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD ✔ (via concept comparisons), concepts & column concepts ✔, metrics dw_488/dw_505/dw_1888/dw_126/dw_12/dw_1357/dw_3280/dw_3867 ✔ (full SQL). **Note: mysql_query failed on every attempt with \"Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'\" — data verification was impossible; the query is grounded entirely in retrieved column definitions and precedent SQL.**\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n**6a.** FCLT_BUILDING_HIST (name, fiscal period, per-period assignable area, campus sector, ext gross area, ACADEMIC/OWNED/MIT filters, Stata exclusion by key) ⨝ FCLT_ROOMS ⨝ FCLT_MAJOR_USE (MAJOR_USE IN ('RESIDENT','LABS'), SUM(AREA)).\n**6b.** Group by building name + fiscal period (plus functionally dependent hist columns), HAVING SUM(r.AREA) > 1000; running sum as `SUM(ASSIGNABLE_AREA) OVER (PARTITION BY CAMPUS_SECTOR ORDER BY FISCAL_PERIOD, BUILDING_NAME)` (window over grouped rows, matching dw_3280 pattern and the requested final ordering); ORDER BY FISCAL_PERIOD, BUILDING_NAME. Caveat: FCLT_ROOMS is a current snapshot, so room areas repeat across the 48 periods — this is the documented precedent behavior (dw_488).\n**6c.** Data: only hist has FISCAL_PERIOD/per-period CAMPUS_SECTOR/EXT_GROSS_AREA; FCLT_ROOMS_HIST covers a single period. Semantic-network: concept decision guides route per-fiscal-period questions to FCLT_BUILDING_HIST; MAJOR_USE codes 'RESIDENT'/'LABS' verbatim in FCLT_MAJOR_USE desc. Business: dw_488 (identical join+filter shape), dw_1888 (Stata exclusion), dw_3280 (running-sum window).\n**6d.** Alternative: filtering on FCLT_BUILDING (current classification) instead of hist — rejected because the question's grain is per-fiscal-period and dw_488 (the closest room-area precedent) filters on the hist table.\n\n",
